{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And Elohim said to Noah, the end of all flesh</b>. It is the body." "And the sense of בא [has come]: their calamity's end has arrived." "<b>את הארץ [the earth]</b>. [Meaning] from the earth, and likewise כצאתי את העיר (Exodus 9:29); or [את meaning] 'with,' as in את יעקב איש וביתו (ibid. 1:1). But the correct view in my eyes is that the word משחיתם [I will destroy them] draws itself and another with it, and likewise אלהים צבאות (Psalms 80:8), כסאך אלהים (ibid. 45:7). And so it is: 'and I will destroy them and destroy the earth.'"], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {2 "The phrase 'draws itself and another with it' renders Ibn Ezra's grammatical point about a word governing both a reflexive and an additional object; left compressed as in the original."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:43:32.815807398Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}